    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (74.65) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.23) stand as our clear offensive anchors. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play; while facing a solid arm in Kevin Gausman, his elite sprint speed against a slow-working battery creates a premium environment for stolen bases, netting him a massive 86% SB efficiency boost in our model. **Seiya Suzuki** similarly benefits from a high-leverage spot in the #2 hole against Merrill Kelly. Kelly\u2019s high xERA (5.27) provides a target-rich environment, and **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s placement at the top of the order ensures he capitalizes on both base-running opportunities and run-scoring potential. \n\nThe optimizer leaned heavily into matchup-specific efficiency, particularly with **Mickey Moniak**, whose 57.96 score is buoyed by a significant +14% platoon advantage. Conversely, the benching of **Griffin Conine** (35.12) was the most difficult decision of the morning. While **Griffin Conine** flashed a strong 0.383 xwOBA, his placement in the #8 spot and the negative platoon splits against Ranger Suarez dropped him below the threshold for a start. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Max Muncy**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Zach McKinstry**, as all remain \"Lineup Pending.\" Specifically, **Zach McKinstry** (41.67) occupies a precarious position; while the wind blowing out offers a slight +5% boost, he faces the toughest path to value given his lower base projection and the high-skill ceiling of Drew Rasmussen. Keep a close eye on final lineup cards, as any move out of the projected order could force a re-evaluation of these marginal starts.",
